    "reason": "[ev-8aa9ac2ddd3a] says the default of `CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool.spec.allowFirstLastIPs` is now `yes`, so the first and last IPs become allocatable \"unless explicitly configured otherwise\". That means a pool where the field is unset is exposed, and a pool that sets the field explicitly is shielded. The proposed exposure (a cilium.io CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool with the field unset) and overlap (the field set) follow the standard pattern for a CRD-field default change. The CRD validator confirmed that cilium.io CiliumLoadBalancerIPPool spec.allowFirstLastIPs exists in both releases [ev-0b16ef08fe62, ev-f958ebb9b848].",
